{
  "_schema": "phantasie.graphics-pack/v1",
  "_note": "Apple II Phantasie I art (VERSION 1.0; the p1-apple2 import, P1Apple2Art; reverse-engineering/apple2/phantasie1/GRAPHICS.md). Every picture is an Applesoft shape (SHAPES, 58 shapes) drawn at the game's SCALE / HCOLOR and turned into colour by an NTSC artifact model [~], except the title picture (HPIC). I's engine is II's Apple engine, so the pack is laid out as II's. The Apple's text is the ROM font (not on the disks): the remaster 5x7 font stands in. Screen kept at the remaster's 320 x 200 layout: Apple pictures (280 x 192 hi-res pixels) are drawn 1:1 in it. Map: the Apple draws its 20 x 26 map rotated against the remaster's 26 x 20 grid (FORMAT.md 3.6); here the tiles follow the remaster's grid, 22 x 20 cells of 7 x 6. A tile's colour fringes depend on its screen column on the Apple: the pack uses the even-column look. No town, item, ending or defeat pictures: the Apple's town is text; CEMETARY / FLASH? draw in BASIC, replayed from apple2_scenes (s224).",
