  "apple2_field": {
    "_note": "OUTDOORS / DUNGON (the same lines) 1480-2006, 4100-4145, 4790-4811; GRAPHICS.md section 7. The round (1560-2005) plays on the mixed hi-res screen (graphics rows 0-159, text rows 20-23: POKE 34,20); the status, ranks, PARTY OPTIONS and orders (1000-1470) are a TEXT page, the remaster's screen there. Lines: the set-up's HPLOTs (4810), white; the field is left of x 138, the map right of it (not drawn here, black [~]). Party: slot k's body + arm at (19k, 158) (1525-1534; dead members not drawn, the slot kept), arm 22 from a swing (1695), 21 from a cast (1760) or a parry that took (1532), else 20; bodies by TOWN 2350-2356. Monsters: front rank y 135, next 135 - YS% of the front, third that - YS% of the second, not below 0 (1480-1500); monster i of n at H% + INT(i * 120 / n) (1550); pose B (S% + 1) from its swing, cast or breath to the round's end (2006); erased at its DIES (4145). The sparkle (23) at (19k + 19, 136) during the cast tones (1762-1764), the spell hit (24) at the monster's SCALE for 500 loops (4132). H%, SCALE, YS% and each picture's DRAW point are the Apple's data: the import's extraction-index.json (index). Pauses: PA = 120 * TIME LAG loops a line (361 / 7560); loop_ms is a rule of thumb for an empty Applesoft FOR / NEXT pass [~]; sparkle_ms the cast tones' length (CALL 770 not decoded) [?].",
