    "_note": "s224 (GRAPHICS.md 8): CEMETARY (defeat) and FLASH? (ending) as their BASIC runs them, a statement per step and s = the seconds to the next statement (the Apple II+ ROM run in a 6502 emulator, 1.020484 MHz; a key wait's s runs after the key). Drawn on a hi-res page with the ROM's DRAW / XDRAW (any ROT) / HPLOT and SHAPES (shapes.bin). Mixed mode: hi-res rows 0-159 over text rows 21-24. The party row: CEMETARY 630 draws shape 19 + 20 at X = 65 TO 185 STEP 120 / (PO + (PO = 0)) (two figures for a lone member); FLASH? 40-50 the member's own body (record byte 168, bodies) after arm 20 at 35 + PM * 180 / PO (120 alone). The fates are Core's (CEMETARY's own rule, 725-740, is not used); their seconds are the Apple's per path. Not shown: DUNGON's INSERT BOOT DISK page before CEMETARY, FLASH?'s after the scene. Interpreter times vary with the party (names, bodies) [~]; page 2 (flash) is rebuilt from SHAPES and FLASH? only [~].",
